-- Industry Scenario Lab: hypothetical practice problems. They are never personal experience.
insert into public.interview_scenarios (slug, domain, title, situation, task, difficulty, model_approach) values
('upi-failure-spike','Payments','Spike in failed UPI transactions',
 'Between 7 PM and 9 PM yesterday, UPI payment success rate for your merchants dropped from 96% to 81%. Merchants are complaining and the support queue has tripled.',
 'Explain how you would investigate, contain and communicate this incident.','intermediate',
 '["Confirm the scope: which merchants, banks (issuer/acquirer), apps and amount bands are affected","Split failures by response code: technical declines (timeouts, U30/U69-type bank errors) vs business declines (insufficient funds, wrong PIN)","Check NPCI and partner bank status pages and incident channels; compare against the same window last week","Contain: route traffic away from a failing PSP/bank if smart routing exists; inform merchants with an ETA","Reconcile: identify transactions stuck in pending/deemed-success and make sure auto-reversals or refunds happen within TAT","Communicate: incident summary to stakeholders, root cause, customer impact, and prevention actions","Prevent: alert thresholds on success rate by bank, runbook updates"]'),
('settlement-mismatch','Payments','Merchant settlement mismatch',
 'A large merchant says their settlement for Monday is short by ₹3.4 lakh compared with their own sales report.',
 'Walk through how you would reconcile and resolve the gap.','intermediate',
 '["Get the merchant''s transaction-level report and the settlement report for the same cut-off window","Match on transaction IDs/RRN; separate timing differences (T+1 cut-off), refunds, chargebacks, MDR/GST deductions and failed transactions","Check for transactions captured after the cut-off that roll into the next settlement","Check holds/reserves applied by risk or compliance","Quantify each bucket so the ₹3.4 lakh is fully explained","Raise a ticket with the acquiring bank for any unexplained remainder; share a clear breakup with the merchant","Fix the root cause: clearer settlement reports, cut-off communication"]'),
('revenue-decline','Business Operations','Declining monthly revenue',
 'Revenue from your top city fell 12% month on month while other cities grew.',
 'How would you find the cause and recommend actions?','intermediate',
 '["Validate the data first: same definitions, no reporting or tracking change","Decompose revenue = customers x orders per customer x average order value; find which driver moved","Segment by channel, product, customer cohort, and new vs returning","Check external factors: competitor launch, pricing change, seasonality, outages, supply issues","Talk to on-ground teams and a sample of churned customers","Recommend 2-3 targeted actions with expected impact and how you will measure them"]'),
('sla-deterioration','Operations','Onboarding SLA deterioration',
 'Merchant onboarding turnaround has slipped from 3 days to 7 days over two months.',
 'Diagnose the slowdown and propose a plan.','intermediate',
 '["Map the process end to end and measure time spent in each stage (KYC, document checks, bank approval, device dispatch)","Find the bottleneck stage and whether it is volume, rework or a dependency","Check rework rate: incomplete documents, KYC rejections; fix at the source with checklists","Balance capacity: queue prioritisation, cross-training, automation of repetitive checks","Agree SLAs with partner banks and track them weekly","Set a dashboard with leading indicators and a weekly review"]'),
('stakeholder-conflict','Stakeholder Management','Sales and risk disagree',
 'Sales wants a high-volume merchant live this week. Risk wants two more weeks of checks because of an unusual business model.',
 'How would you handle this?','intermediate',
 '["Understand both positions and the actual risk concern; do not pick a side early","Quantify: revenue at stake vs potential loss/regulatory exposure","Look for middle paths: go live with lower limits, rolling reserve, enhanced monitoring","Put the trade-off in writing and escalate to the decision owner if needed","Communicate the decision and timeline clearly to the merchant"]'),
('requirements-gathering','Business Analysis','Gathering requirements for a new dashboard',
 'The operations head asks for "a dashboard that shows how we are doing".',
 'How would you turn this into clear requirements?','beginner',
 '["Identify users and the decisions they need to make","Ask what questions they answer today and how (current reports, spreadsheets)","Define 5-8 metrics with exact definitions, owners and refresh frequency","Agree data sources and data quality checks","Sketch a wireframe, review it, then build an MVP and iterate","Document acceptance criteria"]'),
('data-quality','Data Analysis','Inconsistent numbers between two reports',
 'Finance and Operations both report "monthly active merchants" but their numbers differ by 9%.',
 'How would you resolve this?','intermediate',
 '["Collect both definitions and the SQL/logic behind each","Compare at row level for one month to find where they diverge (filters, time zone, status, duplicates)","Agree a single definition with both owners and document it in a metric glossary","Fix the pipeline and add automated checks","Communicate the change and restate history if needed"]'),
('reporting-error','Data Analysis','A published report had an error',
 'You find that last week''s leadership report overstated collections by 6% because of duplicate rows.',
 'What do you do?','beginner',
 '["Confirm the error and the corrected figure quickly","Inform your manager and the report recipients proactively with the corrected numbers","Find the root cause (join creating duplicates) and fix it","Add a reconciliation check against a control total","Note the lesson learned; do not hide the mistake"]'),
('automation-opportunity','Process Improvement','Manual reconciliation takes 3 hours daily',
 'A team member spends 3 hours every day matching bank statements against internal records in Excel.',
 'How would you evaluate and implement automation?','intermediate',
 '["Document the current steps, inputs, exceptions and volumes","Estimate time saved and error reduction","Choose the simplest tool that works: Excel Power Query, SQL, Python script or an internal tool","Build with exception reporting so humans review only mismatches","Run in parallel with the manual process before switching","Measure results and document the process"]'),
('chargeback-surge','Payments','Chargeback surge for one merchant',
 'One merchant''s chargeback ratio rose from 0.3% to 1.8% in three weeks.',
 'How would you respond?','advanced',
 '["Pull chargeback reason codes and transaction patterns (cards, BINs, amounts, time)","Separate fraud chargebacks from service/delivery disputes","Engage the merchant for evidence and representment where valid","Apply risk controls: velocity limits, 3DS enforcement, reserves","Escalate if card network thresholds are at risk","Monitor weekly until the ratio normalises"]')
on conflict do nothing;
